{"availability":"available","full":"22Nm1a0530/sprintflow-ai","name":"sprintflow-ai","description":"AI-powered project management platform for software teams — built with React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. Features authentication, project tracking, a drag-and-drop Kanban board, and analytics dashboards.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-25T13:29:53Z","updated":"2026-07-27T07:01:04Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sprintflow-ai-eta.vercel.app","topics":["ai","cicd","groq","kanban","project-management","react","supabase","tailwind","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://sprintflow-ai-eta.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.758Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.758Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.758Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.758Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An AI-powered project management platform for software teams. Plan projects, break work into tasks using AI, manage them on a Kanban board, track progress with analytics, and govern your team through role-based access control.","Accounts and password resets live in Supabase because they have a hard requirement to work across devices. A user might request a password reset on a laptop and need to complete it on their phone — that's only possible with a shared database both devices can read.","Projects, tasks, and Kanban data live in localStorage because they don't carry that cross-device requirement for this project's scope. A user manages their board from whichever device they're actively working on. This kept the majority of the app's data layer simple and fast to build, while solving the one place where a shared backend was genuinely necessary."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/22Nm1a0530/sprintflow-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"45f649e9aa81f05db448babcc18ebb7d1fcd8a3cd0930bc5235fa1bc638